# Hardhat — Arc Testnet deployer key (never commit real .env)
# Official network: https://docs.arc.network/integrate/connect-to-arc
#   Chain ID 5042002 · RPC https://rpc.testnet.arc.network · Symbol USDC · Explorer https://testnet.arcscan.app
# Chave de 32 bytes em hex (0x + 64 caracteres). Geração local: npm run wallet:generate
PRIVATE_KEY=
# Gerar uma chave nova só na tua máquina (não colas a saída em chats):
#   npm run wallet:generate

# Official Arc Testnet (see https://docs.arc.io/arc-chain)
# Optional: same RPC for browser (wagmi) and server (API routes)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARC_TESTNET_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.arc.network
# ARC_TESTNET_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.arc.network

# Optional: override on-chain contract from generated files (browser)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARC_GOVERNANCE_ADDRESS=0x...

# Bobbie AI — contract link on Arc Testnet (public address only; optional override)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOBBIE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=0x8Ce26Ce6E76301728f004bBA5706CC3e8B95cd2D

# Bobbie AI — optional extra ERC-20 row in Portfolio (Arc Testnet), e.g. bridged ARC
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARC_ERC20_TOKEN_ADDRESS=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARC_ERC20_DECIMALS=18

# Bobbie AI — multi-asset swap (defaults ship in src/constants/bobbie*.generated.ts after deploy:bobbieswap)
# Override only with a BobbieMultiSwap address (not legacy BobbieArcSwap). If unset, codegen address is used.
# On Vercel: remove stale NEXT_PUBLIC_BOBBIE_SWAP_ADDRESS or set it to the MultiSwap from deploy output.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOBBIE_SWAP_ADDRESS=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOBBIE_ETH_TOKEN_ADDRESS=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOBBIE_WBTC_TOKEN_ADDRESS=0x...

# If you ran deploy against the local Hardhat network for a smoke test,
# reset the committed stub address with: npm run contracts:codegen

# Optional: overrides default `public/sounds/arc audio.mp4` after each confirmed tx
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TX_SUCCESS_SOUND_URL=/sounds/outro.mp3

# Optional: WalletConnect (else injected / MetaMask only)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# Dev — permitir acesso pelo IP da máquina na LAN (evita 403 em assets do Next)
# Ex.: NEXT_ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=192.168.1.7
# Depois: npm run dev:host e abra http://SEU_IP:3000 no celular/outro PC

# Vercel — em Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production/Preview):
#   copie os mesmos NEXT_PUBLIC_* que precisar; nunca coloque PRIVATE_KEY na Vercel.
# Vercel: Root Directory pode ficar em "." (raiz); Next.js está na raiz deste repo.
# CLI (raiz do repo): npm run vercel:login → npm run vercel:link → npm run vercel:prod
